Exceptions

- books/ (DotAny Books) is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
  version 3 or (at your option) any later version: see books/LICENSE. It contains
  DjVu.js (GPL-2.0-or-later), which requires this. The MIT code in shared/ that
  Books is built from stays MIT in its own files; the Books program as a whole is
  GPL.
- Fonts keep their own licences, which are not MIT, and each licence text sits
  beside its font:
  - shared/fonts/: Stack Sans Text and Headline, Noto Sans JP DotAny (Noto Sans
    JP cut to the common kanji and renamed) and Pretendard, under the SIL Open
    Font License 1.1; HarmonyOS Sans SC and TC, under Huawei's HarmonyOS Sans
    Fonts License Agreement (LICENSE-HarmonyOS-Sans.txt), which allows them to
    be redistributed unmodified with software, not on their own.
  - books/fonts/: Noto Serif SC, SIL OFL 1.1.
  - text/fonts/: JetBrains Mono, SIL OFL 1.1; Unscii 16, public domain.
- Third-party code keeps its own licence. Each program lists every library it
  contains, with its licence text, on its Licenses & Credits page. The C and
  JavaScript code kept in this repository carries its licence in its folder:
  LAME 3.100 (LGPL-2.0, shared/sound-encode/vendor/lame-3.100), libFLAC
  (BSD-3-Clause, shared/sound-encode/vendor/flac), libopenmpt (BSD-3-Clause,
  shared/sound/vendor/libopenmpt), libarchive (BSD-2-Clause,
  shared/unpack/vendor/libarchive) and DjVu.js (books/vendor/djvujs). LAME is
  built as a library of its own, libmp3lame.dll on Windows and
  libmp3lame.dylib on the Mac, which the programs load when they run, so it can
  be replaced with one built from its source. The crates under the MPL-2.0 are
  used as published on crates.io, where their source is.
